    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n74346" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀξύ̆-πεινος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>ravenously hungry,
				ravenous, greedy,</i> of the eagle, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				619b29
			</span></i> ; of persons, <i><span class="en">
				Antiph.
				276
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Eub.
				10.4
			</span></i> : metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς τοὺς λόγους ὀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.512f
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Cic.
				<u>Att.</u>
				2.12.2
			</span></i> :—later <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀξῠ-πείνης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, ὁ, of one who eats between meals, <i><span class="en">
				Anon.
				<u>in EN</u>
				182.9
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τένθης λέγεται ὁ ὀ. καὶ
				προτένθης</span> Procl.ad <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Op.</u>
				522
			</span></i>.</div>
